<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>Comparison of exponent difference (<math id="S4.T2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Delta|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Delta|</annotation></semantics></math>) for cross-entropy components. <math id="S4.T2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Delta|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Delta|</annotation></semantics></math> measures the difference in scaling exponent between each component and cross-entropy.
Best values are bolded. Results show that the scaling exponent of Error-Entropy is closest to cross-entropy.</figcaption>
